cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Inter-Agent Disagreement as a Signal of Hallucination in AI Agent-Based Question Answering"
abstract: >-
  A study of whether semantic disagreement between two role-conditioned LLM
  agents can serve as a reliable signal of hallucination risk, evaluated on the
  full 817-question TruthfulQA generation split with a judge-graded, fair
  comparison against a single-model Qwen 3 32B baseline. Main finding: inter-agent
  disagreement does NOT predict hallucination (a clean, well-powered negative result).
type: software
